# Every value here is optional: a foundry-data volume holding the build the
# pinned image asks for runs with none of them.
#
# The cache is keyed to an exact filename, foundryvtt-<version>.zip, so bumping
# the image in docker-compose.yml leaves the volume warm for the wrong version.
# docs/how-to/verify-foundry-module-with-docker-compose.md covers each way to
# fill it.

# Credentials. Keep these in one file outside the checkout so every worktree
# shares it, and pass it with `docker compose --env-file <path> up`. With
# 1Password, set each to an op:// reference and run
# `op run --env-file <path> -- docker compose up` instead.
#
# With a username and password the container downloads the pinned build
# itself. The license key is applied on first run; the admin key locks the
# /setup screens and is safe to omit on localhost.
FOUNDRY_USERNAME=
FOUNDRY_PASSWORD=
FOUNDRY_LICENSE_KEY=
# FOUNDRY_ADMIN_KEY=

# Fallbacks without credentials. Compose reads these from .env in the checkout
# (gitignored).

# A timed download link for the Foundry build. Generate it from your Foundry
# account -> Purchased Software Licenses -> set OS to "Node.js" -> click the
# timed URL button. It expires, so generate it right before `docker compose
# up`.
# FOUNDRY_RELEASE_URL=

# Install a build whose version differs from the pinned image's. The container
# warns about the mismatch and proceeds.
# FOUNDRY_VERSION=
